@startuml
title Lifecycle of a Rholang-Authored Language Specification
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam sequenceArrowColor #334155
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #64748B

participant "Rholang\nprocess" as P #E0E7FF
participant "spec value\n<latex>v</latex>" as V #E0E7FF
participant "elaborator\n<latex>\mathcal{E}</latex>" as E #FDE68A
participant "validator\n<latex>\mathcal{V}</latex>" as VAL #FDE68A
participant "identity\n<latex>\mathcal{F}</latex>" as FP #FBCFE8
participant "versioned\nregistry" as REG #DDD6FE
participant "backend\ngenerators" as BE #DCFCE7
participant "RSpace /\nFLT resolver" as RS #BFDBFE

== 1. Construction (pure — no COMM) ==
P -> V : build nested List / Map / String literals
note right of V #E0E7FF
  Constructing a spec is **value construction**.
  No send, no receive, no name creation.
  Two processes building the same spec
  produce <latex>\alpha</latex>-identical values.
end note

== 2. Elaboration and validation (fail-closed) ==
P -> E : <latex>\mathcal{E}(v)</latex>
E -> E : canonicalize (sort option keys,\nreject unknown tags)
E --> P : <latex>\texttt{Err(SpecError)}</latex> on any malformed node
E -> VAL : <latex>\texttt{LanguageDef}</latex>
VAL -> VAL : <latex>\texttt{validate\_language}</latex> +\ncomposition + auto-injection +\nstratification
VAL --> P : <latex>\texttt{Err(ValidationError)}</latex> with a **value path**,\nnot a Rust <latex>\texttt{Span}</latex>

== 3. Identity ==
VAL -> FP : augmented <latex>\texttt{LanguageDef}</latex>
FP -> FP : <latex>\mathcal{F} = \texttt{mettail-langdef-v1:}\mathrm{fnv1a64}(\mathrm{ident}(d))</latex>
note right of FP #FBCFE8
  Identical to the macro path:
  <latex>\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{E}(v)) = \mathcal{F}(\texttt{parse}(s))</latex>
  whenever <latex>v</latex> and <latex>s</latex> denote the same language.
end note

== 4. Registration ==
FP -> REG : <latex>\texttt{insertVersion(ret, "lib", deployer, id, ver, }v\texttt{)}</latex>
REG --> P : <latex>\texttt{rho:lib:1.*:}\langle\mathit{pk}\rangle\texttt{:}\langle\mathit{id}\rangle\texttt{:}\langle\mathit{ver}\rangle</latex>

== 5. Installation ==
REG -> BE : <latex>\texttt{LanguageDef}</latex>
BE -> RS : <latex>\texttt{rhoapi::Par}</latex> driver network,\nset-automaton pattern DAG
BE -> RS : reflected head tags <latex>\ulcorner \mathcal{F}\cdot L \urcorner</latex>

== 6. Use ==
P -> RS : FLT <latex>\texttt{L`term`}</latex> resolved by <latex>\mathcal{F}</latex>
RS --> P : reduced reflected term
@enduml
